  "rationale": "I scored each output against the seven scorecard criteria and recomputed every total from its criterion points: A 91, C 90, B 85.\n\nAll three outputs are read-only, label the evidence honestly as coming from the static description, and correctly decline to give a numeric score. A wins narrowly. Its type, spacing, radius and elevation corrections are the most implementation-ready. Every redesign move maps to a finding, and its validation plan is tightly scoped. C is nearly as good: its next-hour filter is the most operationally specific, but its visual-craft guidance is a little less precise. B is competent but less specific on surface craft, and its validation plan is slightly heavier than needed.",
